From: rocjitsu vfio-user development
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: stub amdgpu_amdkfd_drm_client_create for vfio-user

amdgpu_amdkfd_drm_client_create is called from amdgpu_pci_probe during
device initialization. It creates a DRM client for KFD internal use by
calling drm_client_init → amdgpu_driver_open_kms → amdgpu_vm_init.

In vfio-user emulation adev->vm_manager is not fully initialized at the
point amdgpu_vm_init+0x359 accesses it (mov 0x1c8(%r13),%rax with r13=0),
causing a NULL pointer dereference (CR2: 0x1c8) that crashes the probe.

Stub this function to return 0 immediately. KFD topology registration and
device discovery still work; the DRM client is needed only for KFD internal
GPU memory operations which are not yet supported in vfio-user emulation.

The call stack for the crash:
  amdgpu_vm_init+0x359
  amdgpu_driver_open_kms
  drm_file_alloc
  drm_client_init
  amdgpu_amdkfd_drm_client_create
  amdgpu_pci_probe+0x325

Applies to: ROCm amdgpu roc-7.2.x
Tested on:  kernel 7.0.0-28-generic, Ubuntu 24.04 Noble

--- a/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd.c
+++ b/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_amdkfd.c
@@ -139,6 +139,10 @@ void amdgpu_amdkfd_device_probe(struct amdgpu_device *adev)

 int amdgpu_amdkfd_drm_client_create(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
+	/* vfio-user emulation: adev->vm_manager not fully initialized at probe
+	 * time; stub out to avoid NULL dereference in amdgpu_vm_init+0x359. */
+	return 0;
+
 	if (!adev->kfd.init_complete || adev->kfd.client.dev)
 		return 0;
